<!--
  compute-sanitizer suppressions for the RoLA sanitize lane.

  A SUPPRESSION IS A RECORDED DECISION, NOT A CONVENIENCE. Every entry states which
  finding it silences, in whose code, and why that finding is not ours to fix. An
  entry with no reason is a defect: the whole value of running the tool is that a
  finding means something, and an unexplained suppression converts a real report into
  a silence nobody can audit later.

  EMPTY IS THE CORRECT STATE UNTIL A FINDING IS TRIAGED. The file exists and is passed
  on every invocation so that adding an entry is a reviewable diff rather than a flag
  someone appends to a command line. A whole TOOL that reports a structural false
  positive belongs in `sanitize.py`'s SKIP table with its reason, not here: a
  per-location suppression for a structural cause rots the moment the code moves.

  The root element name is the tool's, verified by running it: a file with any other
  root is refused with "Error reading ...: No such node (ComputeSanitizerOutput)" on
  every invocation, which is a broken lane that still exits zero.
-->
